📌 README — Language School Management System (Python + SQLAlchemy)
🎯 Overview
This project is a Language School Management System built with Python, SQLAlchemy ORM, and SQLite.
The system manages:

Student registration

IELTS & Speaking course tracking

Remaining session management

Backup system

User login & admin authentication

Full CRUD operations

Clean multi-layer architecture (DAL, BL, Models)

The project is designed with a clean, scalable, and maintainable structure, suitable for real-world educational centers.

🏛 Project Architecture
Code
📦 LanguageSchoolApp
 ┣ 📂 BE
 ┃ ┗ 📄 Setting.py
 ┣ 📂 DAL
 ┃ ┗ 📄 Repository.py
 ┣ 📂 BL
 ┃ ┗ 📄 blPersonal.py
 ┣ 📂 Models
 ┃ ┗ 📄 Personal.py
 ┣ 📄 main.py
 ┗ 📄 README.md
✔ BE (Back-End Settings)
Contains database configuration and connection string.

✔ DAL (Data Access Layer)
Implements a clean, reusable Repository Pattern with:

Add

Read / ReadById

Update (Dynamic)

Delete

Search (Dynamic)

Reports

Login

Duplicate checking

Backup operations

All methods use SQLAlchemy Session Management with proper error handling.

✔ BL (Business Logic Layer)
Contains business rules and validation logic.
BL does not directly access the database; it communicates only through the Repository.

✔ Models
SQLAlchemy ORM models for:

Personal

BakPersonal

Login

All models follow clean conventions and include __repr__ for debugging.

🧩 Features
🔹 Student Management
Register new students

Update student information

Delete student records

Search by any field

Track IELTS & Speaking sessions

Track remaining sessions

🔹 Backup System
Every deleted student can be stored in BakPersonal for recovery.

🔹 Reporting
Report by exact date

Report by date range

Dynamic search filters

🔹 Authentication
Login system

Admin flag (isAdmin)

Secure credential checking

🔹 Clean Architecture
Separation of concerns

Reusable repository

Scalable BL layer

ORM-based models

Easy to extend

🛠 Technologies Used
Technology	Purpose
Python 3.x	Main programming language
SQLAlchemy ORM	Database mapping & CRUD
SQLite	Lightweight database
Repository Pattern	Clean DAL architecture
Layered Architecture	Maintainability & scalability


📂 Database Models
Personal
Stores student information and course progress.

BakPersonal
Backup table for deleted students.

Login
User authentication & admin access.

🚀 How to Run
bash
pip install sqlalchemy
python main.py
Database will be automatically created using:

python
Base.metadata.create_all(engine)
